# Real production paperwork (Never commit raw confidential assets).
# Third-party call sheets, camera reports and script logs are copyrighted and
# routinely carry crew personal data, so they stay out of the repository.
# Point CINESPINE_EXAMPLES_DIR at a local copy instead.
data/raw/
data/staging/

# The contents rather than the directory itself, so the synthetic fixtures
# below can be named back in. Git never looks inside a directory it has
# excluded, and an exception underneath one is silently dead.
data/examples/*
*.pdf
*.cif
*.kdm
*.db
spine.db
# WAL mode keeps two sidecar files beside the database. They hold committed
# data that has not been checkpointed yet, so they are as local as the db.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backups/

# The demo fixtures are the exception, and only these: we generate them, they
# describe an invented production, and no clause about real paperwork applies.
# Last in the file so they survive the extension rules above -- the timecode
# log is a .pdf.
#
# Excluded, they were skipped in silence. `demo_inject_events` reads the
# examples directory by filename and passes over what is not there, so a clone
# without a local copy ingested no offload evidence at all and still reported
# the demo injected successfully.
!data/examples/DEMO_*
!data/examples/demo_*


# Local code-intelligence indexes (rebuilt on demand, machine-specific)
.codegraph/
graphify-out/
gcp-credentials.json

# Cloud Run deployment env, which names the ClickHouse host and is per-deployment.
deploy/cloudrun.env.yaml
